{
  "$comment": "VAPP-200 (docs/spec/apps.md §9.2): a READ-ONLY surface (`SurfaceSettings.readOnly`, catalog/host.json surface): the viewer may read, not write (an app at app access `read`). Every renderer paints the WRITING controls as if their author had written `disabled: true`, with the components' own disabled look. A writing control: a node with an `on.<event>` action whose `functionCall.call` writes (`records_*`, `actions_*`); a form field (Input, Textarea, NumberField, Checkbox, Radio, ChoiceTiles, Switch, Select, ChipInput, DatePicker, DateRangePicker, TimePicker, FileUpload, Slider) WITHOUT an action of its own (what it edits feeds a later write). A node whose own actions are all pure or host calls (`set`, `bind`, `openUrl`, a host namespace other than `actions.`) stays live: a month Select that `bind`s a query, a filter that `set`s, a dialog's open button. Per case, reduce `node` with the core catalog (templates lifted), then: `disabled` = the ids the read-only pass disables, pre-order (slots before children), the root first, then each lifted template in key order (TS `readOnlyDisabledIds`, Rust `read_only::disabled_ids`; an author's literal `disabled: true` is already disabled and not listed). A PAINTING runner mounts the case with `readOnly` on and checks every `inert` id paints disabled (the read-only ones plus what a disabled Form disables inside it and what the author disabled) and every `live` id paints enabled; and, with `readOnly` off, that the ids of `disabled` paint enabled.",
  "cases": [
